<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!-- Hardened runtime, NOT App Sandbox (ADR 0007): the app spawns pnpm/astro and writes
       ~/CruxGarden directly, so the sandbox-only keys (network.server, files.user-selected,
       network.client) do not apply and are omitted — an unsandboxed process already has them.

       Only what Electron itself needs:
       - allow-jit + allow-unsigned-executable-memory: V8 generates and executes machine code.

       Deliberately absent:
       - disable-library-validation: every dylib/.node we dlopen (better_sqlite3.node, Electron
         frameworks) is inside the bundle and signed with the app identity by electron-builder.
         pnpm, astro and ffmpeg are separate child processes via execFile, not loaded libraries,
         so library validation never sees them.
       - allow-dyld-environment-variables: nothing sets DYLD_* for the main process; leaving it
         on would let anything in the environment inject code into a signed app. -->
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key><true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key><true/>
</dict>
</plist>
